# MiniMax H3 prompt presets — one env file for this entire prompt category
H3_PRESET_FAMILY="transition_language"
H3_PRESETS_JSON={"Crash Zoom":"Use a rapid controlled zoom to a matching detail, then emerge from that detail in the incoming shot.","Cross Dissolve":"Use a restrained cross dissolve with aligned subject placement and a gradual atmospheric blend between shots.","Dip to Black":"Briefly dip through black, preserve continuing sound and reveal the next shot from the same narrative beat.","Dip to White":"Use a short luminous dip to white motivated by a bright source, then resolve smoothly into the next shot.","Doorway Passage":"Move through a doorway or portal that naturally replaces the outgoing environment with the incoming scene.","Dust Burst":"A short physical dust burst masks the cut and settles naturally into the incoming environment.","Fade Through Color":"Fade through a dominant scene color shared by both shots while preserving rhythm and visual orientation.","Film Burn":"Use a brief organic film-burn flare that consumes the outgoing frame and exposes the incoming image without lingering.","Foreground Occlusion":"Cut while the camera passes behind a wall, person or prop, maintaining identical camera direction after the occlusion.","Glitch":"Use a very brief controlled digital glitch at the cut; preserve subject identity and avoid persistent image corruption.","Graphic Shape Wipe":"Use a clean designed geometric shape to cover the frame and reveal the next shot with exact timing.","Hard Cut":"Use a clean hard cut at the exact cue with matched screen direction and uninterrupted action continuity.","Ink Wipe":"A graphic ink shape spreads across the outgoing image and retracts to reveal the next shot with tactile edges.","J-Cut / L-Cut":"Let the incoming sound begin before the visual cut or let outgoing sound continue after it, preserving natural audio continuity.","Lens Flare Wipe":"A bright lens flare travels across frame and masks a seamless cut at peak intensity.","Light Leak":"A motivated light leak sweeps across the lens, briefly obscures the frame and reveals the next shot beneath it.","Luma Fade":"Transition according to image luminance, allowing highlights or shadows to reveal the incoming shot progressively.","Match Cut":"Match shape, composition, color or subject position across the cut so both shots connect as one visual idea.","Match-on-Action":"Cut during a clearly readable action and continue the same movement, speed and direction in the incoming shot.","Morph Match":"Morph only one matched subject or shape across the transition while keeping scale, position and lighting coherent.","Object Wipe":"A foreground object fully crosses the lens and hides a cut to a matched object or movement in the next shot.","Page Turn":"The outgoing frame bends and turns like a page while the incoming shot remains spatially stable underneath.","Paper Tear":"A physical paper-tear edge opens across the frame and exposes the next scene as a layered surface beneath it.","Pixel Dissolve":"Break the outgoing image into restrained pixels that reorganize into the incoming shot while maintaining silhouette readability.","Rack-Focus Cut":"Rack focus onto a foreground or background detail and cut at maximum blur to a matched sharp detail in the next shot.","Smoke Wipe":"A motivated layer of smoke crosses the lens and reveals the incoming scene through changing density.","Speed Ramp":"Accelerate the final movement into the cut and decelerate the matched incoming movement to normal speed.","Spin Transition":"Rotate the camera around a stable center and hide the cut in directional rotational blur without disorienting geography.","Split-Screen Merge":"Introduce both shots in split screen, align their shared subject or horizon and merge into the incoming full frame.","Water Ripple":"A single water-ripple distortion expands across the image and resolves into the next shot without warping subjects afterward.","Whip Pan":"End with a fast whip pan and begin the next shot in the same direction, using motion blur to hide the cut.","Zoom Through":"Push through a clearly defined object or surface and continue the same forward camera path in the next environment."}
